```

### If the `reviewer-haiku` agent does not exist
`reviewer-haiku` is an optional agent (the standard `reviewer` forbids Haiku). Check the
agents file (`agents:` in `.ao/config.yaml`, usually `specs/agents.json`) BEFORE emitting.
If `reviewer-haiku` is absent, emit exactly ONE review per ladder task instead of the
review lenses: `review-spec-<tid>` with `"agent": "reviewer"` (NO `model` — it inherits
the stronger model), the `spec` brief only, same instruction/inputs/outputs shape.
`impl2`/`verify` then list that single review. Never put `model: haiku` on `reviewer`.

## Aggregator — exactly one, as in `breakdown-contract.md` with these changes
```json
{"id": "aggregate-epic-tasks", "agent": "manager",
  "instruction": "workflows/routed-runner/instructions/67-haiku-aggregate.md",
  "depends_on": ["retest-<tid-1>", "...retest-<tid> for each ladder task...",
                 "test2-<tid-c>", "...test2-<tid> for each CRITICAL (standard-pipeline) task..."],
  "inputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/tasks/<tid-1>/test-pass-3.md", "...ladder tasks (test-pass-3.md)...",
             "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/tasks/<tid-c>/test-pass-2.md", "...critical tasks (test-pass-2.md)..."],
  "outputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/all-tasks-complete.md"],
  "timeout_seconds": 3600, "skip_if_outputs_exist": false}
```
The output path and id are unchanged: `full-test` waits on exactly that path.

## Cross-task dependencies
If task B builds on task A's code, add A's LAST entry to `impl1-<B>`'s `depends_on`
(`retest-<A>` for a ladder task, `test2-<A>` for a critical one), keeping `task-breakdown`.

## Additional hard rules
1. Every `depends_on` id must exist in this manifest (or be `task-breakdown`); ids unique.
2. Only the allowed fields from `breakdown-contract.md`; `model` is allowed ONLY as the
   literal `"haiku"`, ONLY on `impl1`, `test-<angle>`, `impl2` and `verify` of a ladder task.
   Never on the aggregator, `impl3`, `retest`, `reviewer`, or any critical-task entry.
3. Count total emitted entries against the cap ({{ params.max_injected_tasks }}) — leave a
   margin of at least 5.
4. Record in `tasks.md`, per `<tid>`: ladder or CRITICAL (+ why), the angles/lenses used,
   and the brief file paths.
